Subject: [BioC] Loading gal files with marray
Message-ID: <200409091354.i89Ds4Y25669@iobion.com>

 


There are some cases when a gal file has the grid-row-column in this order
as described by the header of the file:

Block\tColumn\tRow\t...

(I think that usually it's Block\tGrid\tColumn\t...)

and in this particular case the function read.Galfile() will read the Row
and Column columns incorrectly.

I've tested this with R 1.9.1 and marray 1.5.14 .

